WEBVTT

00:01.460 --> 00:04.570
Ikusen no namida o koe

00:04.570 --> 00:08.200
Omoi wa kouya o yuku

00:08.200 --> 00:16.130
Itsuka kizu wa ieru kara saa trust myself

00:21.280 --> 00:27.790
Yaketsuku hizashi no moto kimi wa nani omou?

00:27.790 --> 00:33.730
Urei no hitomi wa ima nani o utsusu?

00:33.730 --> 00:42.670
Mayowazu ni irareru no nara
step by step tayasui darou

00:42.670 --> 00:47.440
Kaze no you ni

00:47.440 --> 00:50.510
Ikusen no namida o koe

00:50.510 --> 00:54.120
Akatsuki no kouya o yuku

00:54.120 --> 01:00.560
Itsuka kizu wa ieru kara saa trust myself

01:00.560 --> 01:07.360
Don't be afraid kawaru koto wa
osoreru koto ja nai

01:07.360 --> 01:13.470
Kimi ga kimi de aru naraba will be with you

01:13.470 --> 01:20.210
Odayaka na hi o yume-mite

01:20.210 --> 01:27.440
Michi-naki tabiji wa tsuzuku

01:39.830 --> 01:41.700
It's me.

01:41.700 --> 01:43.630
Today's report, please.

01:45.770 --> 01:47.700
I understand.

01:51.310 --> 01:55.810
A mantle of rainbow-colored
light soars the heavens...

01:55.810 --> 02:00.350
Gallant is the dance of flames
that rend the land asunder...

02:00.350 --> 02:03.510
The roar of the spray in frenzied tumult...

02:05.320 --> 02:09.460
They are all the culmination of deviltry...

02:09.460 --> 02:13.260
Where the crimson essence ultimately leads...

02:14.900 --> 02:16.890
Soon...

02:19.830 --> 02:21.770
Melissa...

02:21.770 --> 02:23.810
That's a pretty gun.

02:23.810 --> 02:25.600
Does it work?

02:26.770 --> 02:28.680
Would you like to try shooting it?

02:28.680 --> 02:31.150
At me?

02:31.150 --> 02:34.450
I don't like jokes like that.

02:34.450 --> 02:35.850
That's too bad.

02:54.800 --> 02:56.400
An unusual place?

02:56.400 --> 03:01.340
Yeah, somewhere that's
sort of... a bit mysterious.

03:01.340 --> 03:02.810
Any place like that around here?

03:02.810 --> 03:06.380
Nah, I've never even heard
of anywhere like that.

03:06.380 --> 03:08.350
Oh, I see.

03:08.350 --> 03:12.450
Oh, if you want to hear strange
stories along those lines...

03:14.660 --> 03:15.960
That grandpa?

03:15.960 --> 03:19.930
Go ask him. But I'll warn you,
he's not right in the head.

03:19.930 --> 03:21.590
What?

03:27.770 --> 03:29.700
An unusual place?

03:29.700 --> 03:32.540
Yup, is there any place like that around?

03:32.540 --> 03:35.340
Every place around here is unusual.

03:35.340 --> 03:38.610
Compared to the city, it's all unusual.

03:38.610 --> 03:42.650
Uh, no, that's not what I meant.

03:42.650 --> 03:44.950
Are you traveling?

03:44.950 --> 03:47.250
Yeah, sort of...

03:48.390 --> 03:53.700
You're greatly mistaken if you think
you'll always get what you're seeking.

03:53.700 --> 03:56.760
You mustn't seek.

03:56.760 --> 04:01.300
R-Right, thanks, Grandpa.
That's good to know.

04:01.300 --> 04:03.670
Take care. May you live a long life.

04:04.970 --> 04:07.710
There's a thing called a witches' village.

04:07.710 --> 04:10.480
Witches... Witches?!

04:10.480 --> 04:14.450
That's it, Grandpa! Where's this village?

04:14.450 --> 04:16.020
H-Hey...

04:16.020 --> 04:18.610
Oh! Sorry.

04:20.990 --> 04:23.020
That way?

04:23.020 --> 04:25.330
Those mountains?

04:25.330 --> 04:27.660
Three mountains over,

04:27.660 --> 04:31.030
and then maybe about
five days by horse carriage.

04:31.030 --> 04:33.900
Three mountains and five
days by horse carriage...

04:33.900 --> 04:35.800
Horse carriage, huh?

04:35.800 --> 04:40.480
That's pretty far. What kind of village is it?

04:40.480 --> 04:42.510
It's not there anymore.

04:42.510 --> 04:44.280
What?

04:44.280 --> 04:45.910
It fell to ruin.

04:45.910 --> 04:48.880
That was about ten years ago.

04:53.320 --> 04:56.060
Fell to ruin? Why?

04:56.060 --> 04:59.460
There was a huge fire.

04:59.460 --> 05:01.660
What about the people who lived there?

05:01.660 --> 05:06.690
Who knows? Died or fled...

05:08.070 --> 05:11.910
Did witches... really exist?

05:11.910 --> 05:16.640
Sure. There were a couple
of them in this town, too.

05:16.640 --> 05:19.050
Witches, who'd come from that village...

05:19.050 --> 05:20.780
Really?

05:20.780 --> 05:25.790
They kept their identities hidden,
so few knew about them, though.

05:25.790 --> 05:31.830
Because that village didn't approve
of any dealings with outsiders.

05:31.830 --> 05:34.450
Where are those people now?

05:55.920 --> 05:57.420
Is that your daughter?

05:57.420 --> 05:59.850
- It's my old lady.
- What?

05:59.850 --> 06:03.960
Zaida. She fell ill when she was still young...

06:03.960 --> 06:07.760
She was such a beautiful girl.

06:07.760 --> 06:09.830
She really was.

06:09.830 --> 06:11.970
Zaida was a witch.

06:11.970 --> 06:13.630
What?

06:33.960 --> 06:37.590
She didn't have much in
the way of magical powers.

06:37.590 --> 06:42.460
Lighting candles, heating water,

06:42.460 --> 06:45.730
matching up the marks on playing cards...

06:45.730 --> 06:49.000
- But the witches of old...
- What?

06:49.000 --> 06:52.140
The skies, the land, the waters...

06:52.140 --> 06:57.010
It seems they could control
everything as they wished.

06:57.010 --> 07:02.550
They apparently used to bring about
abundant harvests with those powers.

07:02.550 --> 07:06.590
They were gods, if you will. Goddesses...

07:06.590 --> 07:09.490
If they used it for good things like that, sure.

07:11.190 --> 07:14.630
But if they used their powers for bad things,

07:14.630 --> 07:17.770
you couldn't call them goddesses.

07:17.770 --> 07:19.900
There's a story in the Scriptures, isn't there?

07:19.900 --> 07:23.870
About a demon who ruled the
world using its evil powers...

07:23.870 --> 07:27.170
If I remember right, it was... the Leviathan...

07:33.920 --> 07:39.790
It seems witches who left the
village gradually lost their powers.

07:39.790 --> 07:42.590
Perhaps this weary world sullied them,

07:42.590 --> 07:46.190
or there was something in that village...

07:49.060 --> 07:51.200
If it's out of curiosity, I'd advise against it.

07:51.200 --> 07:53.840
Life isn't just about forging ahead.

07:53.840 --> 07:58.200
At times, you also need
the courage to turn back.

08:00.580 --> 08:03.240
- Did you find out anything?
- What?

08:03.240 --> 08:05.680
Sort of. Did you buy it?

08:05.680 --> 08:08.680
- Not yet.
- So you like it.

08:08.680 --> 08:12.220
"The incandescent flames of love blazed..."

08:12.220 --> 08:17.230
"However, we no longer even
had the money to buy gas..."

08:17.230 --> 08:19.860
- We don't?
- Unfortunately.

08:19.860 --> 08:21.830
Then I'll go return it.

08:21.830 --> 08:23.660
Do you want to work again?

08:23.660 --> 08:25.570
I suppose so.

08:25.570 --> 08:27.670
We're getting close to Wiñay Marka, after all.

08:27.670 --> 08:29.100
What?

08:29.100 --> 08:31.640
I found out where it is.

08:31.640 --> 08:34.080
- Really?
- Yup!

08:34.080 --> 08:35.240
Nadie!

08:35.240 --> 08:39.650
Come on, you're making me feel hot.

08:39.650 --> 08:42.080
Thanks, Grandpa.

08:42.080 --> 08:44.820
But I have to go.

08:44.820 --> 08:46.720
For her sake.

08:46.720 --> 08:49.950
Because we're sure to find answers there.

08:51.230 --> 08:53.830
Is there something you want to get?

08:53.830 --> 08:58.000
You buy me more than enough
of the things I want.

08:58.000 --> 09:00.070
I thought, for once,

09:00.070 --> 09:04.970
it could be nice to go out
without any purpose in mind.

09:04.970 --> 09:08.040
I think it might rain.

09:08.040 --> 09:09.980
Did you notice?

09:09.980 --> 09:11.750
Inca rose.

09:11.750 --> 09:15.750
It's the first present you ever gave me.

09:15.750 --> 09:17.920
They look good on you, Melissa.

09:17.920 --> 09:20.150
They make you forget the unpleasant past

09:20.150 --> 09:23.290
and awaken passions that
had been lying dormant...

09:23.290 --> 09:26.930
You told me that's the kind
of power these stones have.

09:26.930 --> 09:29.030
I'm surprised you remember.

09:29.030 --> 09:32.100
That's exactly how things
have turned out, Doug.

09:32.100 --> 09:34.330
I'm so happy now.

09:42.980 --> 09:45.180
Let's enjoy our day today.

09:45.180 --> 09:48.950
Yes, let's make it a wonderful day.

09:57.990 --> 10:01.660
- I guess this place was a no-go, too.
- There's no work.

10:01.660 --> 10:05.100
Finding day labor might be rough
in a small town like this.

10:05.100 --> 10:06.800
I should've known.

10:06.800 --> 10:10.970
- Then, we'll do this.
- We won't even be able to buy bread.

10:10.970 --> 10:12.670
Shoot...

10:12.670 --> 10:15.680
Talking about bread is making me hungry.

10:15.680 --> 10:17.140
So straightforward.

10:17.140 --> 10:20.750
Well, excuse me.

10:20.750 --> 10:22.350
You're straightforward, too.

10:22.350 --> 10:25.290
Well, excuse me.

10:25.290 --> 10:27.090
- Bread...
- Lirio...

10:27.090 --> 10:30.120
What's this? You're giving it to us?

10:30.120 --> 10:31.760
Thank you!

10:31.760 --> 10:33.730
Penniless again?

10:33.730 --> 10:37.700
It can't be helped, right?
If you spend it, it goes away.

10:37.700 --> 10:40.740
To be honest, we're actually in the same boat.

10:40.740 --> 10:43.100
So I found a way to make money.

10:43.100 --> 10:45.340
Oh, a bounty?

10:45.340 --> 10:48.110
- Care to do it together?
- What?

10:48.110 --> 10:51.710
It was Lirio's idea.

10:51.710 --> 10:54.650
Thank you. I appreciate it...

10:54.650 --> 10:57.690
...but right now, that's not really...

10:57.690 --> 11:00.120
I know.

11:00.120 --> 11:03.190
- Oh...
- A cat...
- It's a puma.

11:03.190 --> 11:05.730
How about it? It's got a hefty bounty on it.

11:05.730 --> 11:07.960
Wow, you're right. It's amazing.

11:07.960 --> 11:10.730
Why is the cat wanted?

11:10.730 --> 11:12.670
Eight have fallen victim to it already.

11:12.670 --> 11:15.800
Ah-ha, so it's a man-eating kitty.

11:15.800 --> 11:18.740
The bounty will be 50/50. Are you in?

11:18.740 --> 11:21.140
Of course!

11:21.140 --> 11:23.740
Thank you, Lirio.

11:23.740 --> 11:27.980
Oh, no... I was just sort of thinking
you've become so well-mannered.

11:27.980 --> 11:29.850
I am well-mannered.

11:29.850 --> 11:33.020
- You're stepping on my foot.
- You're right.

11:33.020 --> 11:36.120
- Where's your "I'm sorry"?
- Why?

11:36.120 --> 11:38.110
I take back everything I just said.

11:50.040 --> 11:51.940
Where am I?

11:56.780 --> 11:58.240
Ellis...

12:02.750 --> 12:07.120
What's going on... with me?

12:17.770 --> 12:20.930
First, a bird, and now a big kitty, huh?

12:24.040 --> 12:26.810
I don't think that'll work as a weapon.

12:26.810 --> 12:28.340
Weapon?

12:28.340 --> 12:29.980
It's a cat, right?

12:29.980 --> 12:32.750
It's not that kind of
laid-back search for a cat.

12:32.750 --> 12:34.450
Dead or alive?

12:34.450 --> 12:37.050
If anything, more like dead.

12:37.050 --> 12:39.490
I see...

12:39.490 --> 12:41.420
- Could that have been?
- Cat!

12:41.420 --> 12:44.950
Ellis! I just told you...

12:51.530 --> 12:53.830
Lirio! Why?

12:53.830 --> 12:55.830
Were you hiding?

12:58.470 --> 13:00.340
Then...

13:05.050 --> 13:06.550
There it is.

13:06.550 --> 13:08.340
It's huge!

13:15.160 --> 13:17.460
Ricardo!

13:17.460 --> 13:19.330
Better not move.

13:19.330 --> 13:21.120
Leave the rest to me.

13:22.530 --> 13:23.930
Lirio!

13:23.930 --> 13:25.970
Ellis, stop her!

13:25.970 --> 13:28.370
You can't. It's dangerous.

13:28.370 --> 13:30.030
Lirio...

13:32.140 --> 13:36.080
I understand how you feel, but leave this to me.

13:36.080 --> 13:39.240
You take Ricardo to the hospital.

13:41.050 --> 13:45.150
Can you do that? Can I count on you for that?

13:45.150 --> 13:47.020
Good.

13:49.020 --> 13:51.030
You stay behind, too.

13:51.030 --> 13:52.560
I'm coming with you.

13:52.560 --> 13:55.330
- Ellis...
- I'm coming.

13:55.330 --> 13:58.600
- Okay, partner.
- Okay.

13:58.600 --> 14:03.000
Nadie, it's a real wild one. Be careful.

14:03.000 --> 14:04.310
I'll be fine.

14:04.310 --> 14:07.410
Nadie's wilder anyway.

14:07.410 --> 14:09.270
Hey!

14:13.350 --> 14:16.980
Life really is all about the people you meet...

14:41.080 --> 14:43.340
Here is your next set of orders.

14:43.340 --> 14:45.180
Yes, sir.

14:52.950 --> 14:54.460
Sorry for making you wait.

14:54.460 --> 14:56.490
Did you find what you were looking for?

14:56.490 --> 15:00.260
Yes. It had fallen under the seat.

15:00.260 --> 15:01.920
I see.

15:04.330 --> 15:06.370
Pretty, isn't it?

15:06.370 --> 15:09.640
It's no match for your beauty.

15:09.640 --> 15:12.130
That's going too far.

15:16.310 --> 15:19.250
I was sure it came this way, but...

15:26.950 --> 15:28.560
Take that!

15:28.560 --> 15:31.260
Whoa, that scared me.

15:31.260 --> 15:32.660
Thank you, Ellis.

15:32.660 --> 15:34.690
You are quite welcome.

15:43.640 --> 15:46.670
- It's gone.
- So it got away...

15:46.670 --> 15:49.640
I wanted to settle this before night fell...

15:49.640 --> 15:52.130
- Ellis!
- Yessir!

16:04.730 --> 16:06.730
Looks like it got hurt.

16:06.730 --> 16:08.630
This is our chance.

17:00.410 --> 17:03.450
You came, Ellis!

17:03.450 --> 17:06.510
L. A! What's the meaning of this?

17:23.370 --> 17:25.170
The Inca rose...

17:59.510 --> 18:01.610
Ellis!

18:01.610 --> 18:03.780
Ellis...

18:03.780 --> 18:05.810
What's going on?

18:05.810 --> 18:07.800
Ellis!

18:10.550 --> 18:12.790
Ellis?

18:12.790 --> 18:16.620
A mantle of rainbow-colored
light soars the heavens...

18:16.620 --> 18:17.860
What?

18:17.860 --> 18:22.860
Gallant is the dance of flames
that rend the land asunder...

18:22.860 --> 18:27.430
The roar of the spray in frenzied tumult...

18:27.430 --> 18:31.270
They are all the culmination of deviltry...

18:31.270 --> 18:34.680
Where the crimson essence ultimately leads...

18:34.680 --> 18:36.440
It can't be...

18:36.440 --> 18:38.100
Ellis?

19:10.740 --> 19:12.740
Incredible!

19:27.360 --> 19:30.360
Ellis!

19:30.360 --> 19:33.700
Ellis! My goddess!

19:36.470 --> 19:38.370
Ellis...

19:46.180 --> 19:49.420
- Ellis!
- It's no use!

19:49.420 --> 19:52.950
The way Ellis is now, she won't know you!

19:52.950 --> 19:57.250
She's being subjected to a great power
and her soul is being released!

20:14.410 --> 20:15.880
Watch out!

20:23.750 --> 20:25.840
What in the world is that?

21:14.800 --> 21:16.740
What happened?

21:19.470 --> 21:21.000
Nadie...

21:24.950 --> 21:26.780
Nadie?!

21:46.870 --> 21:49.770
Ladies and gentlemen, we have
an announcement to make.

21:49.770 --> 21:53.410
The large hurricane that appeared
in the evening has died out

21:53.410 --> 21:56.680
and we currently have
extremely stable air currents.

21:56.680 --> 22:00.610
Please enjoy your pleasant
journey through the skies.

22:12.430 --> 22:13.890
Doug...

22:20.800 --> 22:22.630
Doug...

22:28.440 --> 22:32.610
Rosenberg has finally...

22:32.610 --> 22:34.410
...made his move.

22:36.550 --> 22:40.350
Owaranai natsu no you ni

22:40.350 --> 22:43.790
Chiranai hana no you ni

22:43.790 --> 22:47.690
Dakishimeta sono ude o

22:47.690 --> 22:55.830
Zutto hanasanaide ite yo

23:02.040 --> 23:05.650
Sugari-tsuite-mitemo

23:05.650 --> 23:11.450
Mune wa mada chigau hakanasa de

23:11.450 --> 23:15.420
Toki no rizumu kazoeteru

23:15.420 --> 23:19.530
Akai hoshi no yoru

23:19.530 --> 23:23.530
Kiete-yuku nukumori

23:23.530 --> 23:27.470
Tsunagi-tometai no yo

23:27.470 --> 23:33.870
Hitomi tojita kimi o

23:33.870 --> 23:37.840
Akogare o kuri-kaeshi

23:37.840 --> 23:41.180
Doko e mo yukenaku-temo

23:41.180 --> 23:45.420
Setsunasa no tachidomaru

23:45.420 --> 23:51.730
Kono hito-toki ga futari no

23:51.730 --> 23:56.720
Subete yo
